steps before script of Export Full DB:

mkdir -p /u02/exports/Full_DB
chown oracle:oinstall /u02/exports/Full_DB 
chmod 775 /u02/exports/Full_DB

CREATE OR REPLACE DIRECTORY FULL_DB_DIR AS '/u02/exports/Full_DB/'; 
GRANT READ, WRITE ON DIRECTORY FULL_DB_DIR TO SYSTEM; 


===========================================script of Export Full DB exp_full_db.sh===========================================
#!/bin/bash

# Oracle environment
export ORACLE_BASE=/u01/app/oracle
export ORACLE_HOME=$ORACLE_BASE/product/19.3.0/db_1
export ORACLE_SID=TEST
export PATH=$ORACLE_HOME/bin:$PATH

# Date variable
DATE=$(date +%Y%m%d)

# Run Data Pump export
expdp "' / as sysdba'" \
  full=y \
  directory=FULL_DB_DIR \
  dumpfile=FULL_DB_${DATE}_%U.dmp \
  logfile=FULL_DB_${DATE}.log \
  parallel=4 \
  compression=ALL \
  content=ALL \


*********Cases I Experienced During Full Data Pump Export************

**ORA-29548:** Java system class reported: release of Java system classes in the database (19.0.0.0.211019 1.8) 
does not match that of the Oracle executable (19.0.0.0.0 1.8).

**Temporary Solution:**
Add the following parameter to the `expdp` command:

`EXCLUDE=JAVA_SOURCE,JAVA_CLASS`

**Final Solution:**
Patch both the Grid Infrastructure Home and the Oracle Home, 
apply the OJVM patch, 
then run `datapatch` to update the database SQL components (CATALOG, CATPROC, CATJAVA, CONTEXT, XDB, etc.), 
synchronize the OJVM Java objects with the Oracle Home binaries, and complete the patch installation.

===========================================script for specific schema exp_B1_db.sh===========================================
#!/bin/bash

# Oracle environment
export ORACLE_BASE=/u01/app/oracle
export ORACLE_HOME=$ORACLE_BASE/product/19.3.0/db_1
export ORACLE_SID=TEST
export PATH=$ORACLE_HOME/bin:$PATH

# Date variable
DATE=$(date +%Y%m%d)

# Base export directory 
BASE_DIR=/u02/exports 
TARGET_DIR=${BASE_DIR}/B1_dp_exp_dir_${DATE} 

# Create target folder 
mkdir -p ${TARGET_DIR} 
chmod 775 ${TARGET_DIR}

# Run Data Pump export
expdp "' / as sysdba'" \
  schemas=B1 \
  directory=B1_DP_EXP_DIR \
  dumpfile=B1_${DATE}_%U.dmp \
  logfile=B1_${DATE}.log \
  parallel=4 \
  compression=ALL \
  content=ALL \

# Move generated files to target folder 
mv ${BASE_DIR}/B1_*.dmp ${TARGET_DIR}/
mv ${BASE_DIR}/B1_${DATE}.log ${TARGET_DIR}/ 

  
----------
DON'T FORGET: to give Execute permission to script file -> chmod 755 filename
